# {metadata.title}

_By {metadata.author} — {metadata.date}_

> {metadata.description}

This post is a `.sveltex` file with **YAML frontmatter**. SvelTeX exports
the frontmatter as `metadata` on the module script, which is accessible
inside the page too — the heading above is literally
`{metadata.title}`.

## Why Deno

The whole showcase is built by **Deno** running Vite. SvelTeX itself is
runtime-agnostic — it is published to both npm and JSR — so the same
preprocessor works whether the build host is Node or Deno.

<Callout type="note">
The `imports` key in this page's frontmatter pulls in the `Callout`
component used here, with no separate script block.
</Callout>

## Frontmatter in practice

Keeping metadata next to the content it describes means the title, author and
tags travel with the page. This post is tagged `deno`, `sveltekit` and
`sveltex`, and a build tool can read those straight from the frontmatter.
